WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.913
Turn customer conversations into next steps your team can review.

2
00:00:04.093 --> 00:00:08.947
Meet Intent, an open-source CRM built around evidence and human decisions.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.439
Start with meeting notes.

4
00:00:12.619 --> 00:00:18.213
Preserve what the customer actually said: they need unified records, and
their budget is not approved yet.

5
00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:20.759
Save the evidence to prepare a follow-up.

6
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.412
Review the extracted facts against their original quotes.

7
00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:30.646
Ask a question in the customer’s context, and follow the answer back to its
supporting evidence.

8
00:00:30.826 --> 00:00:33.142
Your team keeps the final judgment.

9
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.941
Open the proposed action.

10
00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:42.229
Check the recipient and content, edit the draft, then approve the exact
revision you reviewed.

11
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:46.777
A suggestion becomes executable work only through an authorized decision.

12
00:00:48.183 --> 00:00:50.829
Follow the result back into the customer record.

13
00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:56.311
This walkthrough uses fictional data, a deterministic Fixture model, and
simulated delivery.

14
00:00:56.491 --> 00:01:00.388
No real email is sent, and a receipt does not mean a sale is won.

15
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:07.849
Self-host your workspace, choose your model provider, and work in English or
Simplified Chinese.

16
00:01:08.029 --> 00:01:11.179
Your integrations remain under administrator control.

17
00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:16.283
Watch the full tutorial, explore the source, and try Intent.
